## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a scalable, governed, multi-region data lake with reliable ingestion, deduplication, and schema evolution.

## Key Concepts

- Regional ingestion paths and Parquet data lake
- Lake Formation governance and CRR
- Idempotent ingestion with event_id dedup
- Schema evolution via Avro + Glue Schema Registry
- Late data handling and e2e testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode dedupe
async function isDuplicate(event_id){
  const exists = await dynamo.get({PK: event_id});
  if (exists) return true;
  await dynamo.put({PK: event_id, ...});
  return false;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale CRR for thousands of regions?
- How would you monitor data quality drift in this setup?

## Why This Is Asked
Practical beginner task validating end-to-end ingestion, data quality, and cataloging.

## Key Concepts
- S3 event-driven ETL
- Glue Spark/DynamicFrame validation
- Quarantine routing for bad records
- Parquet partitioning by date
- Glue Data Catalog and Athena access

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Glue-like JS snippet for validation
function process(batch){
  const valid=[], quarantined=[];
  for (const r of batch){
    if (r.a != null && r.b != null) valid.push(transform(r));
    else quarantined.push({row:r, validation_reason:'missing_required_fields'});
  }
  writeParquet(valid, datePartition);
  writeJson(quarantined, quarantineBucket);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test schema evolution if new fields are added?
- How would you monitor the quarantine rate and alert if it spikes?
